    "narrative": "The slate is highlighted by **Tyler Freeman** (65.30), **Geraldo Perdomo** (64.78), and **Masyn Winn** (64.02), who serve as our engines today. **Tyler Freeman** benefits from a substantial 14% park factor boost and a favorable matchup against Brady Singer, while **Geraldo Perdomo**\u2019s spot in the #2 hole coupled with Michael McGreevy\u2019s mediocre 4.45 xERA keeps his efficiency high. **Masyn Winn** is our most efficient play against a struggling arm, as the 5.29 xERA of Merrill Kelly provides a massive +19% skill boost. In the outfield, **Dylan Beavers** (61.18) is a standout target; while he is currently projected in the #3 slot against Peter Lambert, his +7% platoon advantage and the general weakness of the opposing starter make him a high-upside play for stolen base volume, a critical need given our aggressive roster strategy.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Ryan Waldschmidt** (49.69) out of the starting five. He narrowly missed the cut behind the collective upside of the outfield group; while his metrics are solid, the projection model dinged him heavily for his assumed #9 spot in the batting order, which suppresses run-scoring potential. We are proceeding with caution as every starter\u2019s order is currently \"Lineup Pending.\" Specifically, **Yainer Diaz** (40.67) and **Cal Raleigh** (53.92) are operating near the bottom of our efficiency thresholds. If their official lineup placements drop further down the order than our current assumptions, we may need to pivot to bench options like **Luis Arraez**, whose elite contact profile provides a safer floor if we decide to sacrifice the power-speed upside of the current utility slots. Ensure game caps are monitored closely, as the gap between our top plays and the bench remains narrow.",
